WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.500
It's interesting that young white men are only 10% of the population, but 98% of the military deaths.

00:07.500 --> 00:09.500
You ask for a stat check and you'll get one.

00:09.500 --> 00:14.900
When you break it down by race, black Americans were actually more likely to die in pretty much every recent war.

00:14.900 --> 00:20.300
For instance, in the Vietnam conflict, black men made up 12.4% of all American deaths.

00:20.300 --> 00:24.200
However, black Americans only made up around 10% of the population.

00:24.200 --> 00:26.800
And this is also true for deaths since 1980.

00:26.800 --> 00:29.100
If you want those stats, you can look them up at the DCAS.

00:29.100 --> 00:33.500
So the claim in that video that young white men make up 90% of the military deaths is false.

00:33.500 --> 00:36.300
And since that video was about privilege, I'm going to go ahead and talk about that.

00:36.300 --> 00:41.000
Looking up USA facts, how many people do you think died in the military in 2022?

00:41.000 --> 00:45.500
The answer is 844 deaths out of all of the armed forces in 2022.

00:45.500 --> 00:49.800
In a total of zero of those deaths were from hostile action or terrorist attacks.

00:49.800 --> 00:54.000
The largest numbers were self-inflicted, accidents, illness, pending, and homicide.

00:54.000 --> 00:56.600
I went ahead and grabbed how many people are a part of the military.

00:56.700 --> 01:00.100
And long story short, if we're just including the active duty military members,

01:00.100 --> 01:04.300
then the death rate is about 65.6 per 100,000 people.

01:04.300 --> 01:08.500
In 2021, black women have had the highest maternal mortality rate in the United States

01:08.500 --> 01:11.500
at 69.9 out of every 100,000 live births.

01:11.500 --> 01:17.000
That means it was actually more dangerous in 2021 for a black woman to give birth.

01:17.000 --> 01:22.700
And it was for the average person to be active duty in the military in 2022.

01:22.700 --> 01:26.200
So for this stat check, I'm going to have to rate that claim completely false.

01:26.200 --> 01:28.800
Thanks for the tag, I'll try to do it as often as I can.

